## What the case asks, and what was actually measured

The case has **no authored steps** in `ck.db` (the 53-character empty-JSON placeholder; see the
campaign queue). TPS row **215 "Re-authentication option" reads `Yes`**. The dispatch set the
objective explicitly: *the interesting measurement is that re-authentication **actually happens
on time**, not that the command is accepted* -- so this case was designed as a **timing
measurement on the wire**, with the feature OFF as the control and the removal proved as well.

**Nothing in the case was graded on `show`.** Every verdict below comes from a timestamped
EAPOL frame table, with the DUT's own counters and log as corroboration.

