**STEP 1 verdict: PASS, and this is the measurement the case exists for.**

| re-auth | EAP-Request/Identity at | interval from the previous one |
| --- | --- | --- |
| #1 | 30.049 s | 30.049 |
| #2 | 60.093 s | 30.044 |
| #3 | 90.141 s | 30.048 |
| #4 | 120.190 s | 30.049 |

**Four re-authentications, every one of them within 49 milliseconds of the configured 30 s**, and
every one completing to `EAP-Success`. Three things are proved beyond the command being accepted:

1. **The authenticator initiates.** Each re-authentication begins with an unsolicited
   `EAP-Request/Identity` **from the switch** -- there is no EAPOL-Start from the supplicant
   after t=0.003 s. The timer is the DUT's.
2. **It is a full re-authentication, not a keepalive.** Each cycle runs Identity -> MD5-Challenge
   -> Response -> Success with a **fresh challenge** (four different digests) and a **new EAP
   id pair** (3/4, 5/6, 7/8, 9/10). The server is consulted every time.
3. **The 1.00 s server round-trip is reproduced exactly** on every cycle (1.023, 1.016, 1.019,
   1.018, 1.015 s from MD5 response to Success) -- the same figure group A measured.

## STEP 2 -- the period is honoured, not a fixed timer: change 30 -> 60 and the interval changes

The discriminator that separates "re-authentication happens" from "the configured value is what
drives it". Only `auth timeout reauth-period` was changed; everything else was identical.

```
configure terminal / interface port1.0.48 / auth timeout reauth-period 60 / end
show auth interface port1.0.48 | include reAuth  ->  reAuthenticate: enabled / reAuthPeriod: 60
```

```
pcap -> /tmp/authm1304/T33374-S2.pcap (16 EAPOL frames)
     0.010 <- EAP-Request/Identity id=1       1.025 <- EAP-Success id=2
    60.080 <- EAP-Request/Identity id=3      61.096 <- EAP-Success id=4
   120.148 <- EAP-Request/Identity id=5     121.164 <- EAP-Success id=6
RESULT T33374-S2-reauth-ON-period-60: 1/1 supplicant(s) matched their expectation -- MATCH
```

**STEP 2 verdict: PASS.** Intervals **60.070 s** and **60.068 s** -- within 70 ms of the
configured 60 s. Taken with STEP 0 and STEP 1 this is a **three-point curve on one otherwise
identical leg**, which no accident produces:

| `reauth-period` | listening window | EAPOL frames | authentications | measured interval |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| OFF (`no auth reauthentication`) | 106 s | **6** | 1 | n/a |
| 60 s | 139 s | **16** | 3 | 60.070, 60.068 |
| 30 s | 139 s | **26** | 5 | 30.049, 30.044, 30.048, 30.049 |
| 15 s (STEP 3) | 88 s | **31** | 6 | 15.013 .. 15.030 |

The frame count is a straight function of the configured period and of nothing else.

