## STEP 4 -- REMOVAL: `no auth reauthentication` stops it, with the period still configured

The removal leg was deliberately run with **`auth timeout reauth-period 15` still in place**, so
that the test is specifically of `no auth reauthentication` and not of the period having been
cleared.

```
configure terminal / interface port1.0.48 / no auth reauthentication / end

show running-config interface port1.0.48
!
interface port1.0.48
 switchport
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 48
 dot1x port-control auto
 dot1x control-direction both
 auth timeout reauth-period 15        <-- still there
!
show auth interface port1.0.48 | include reAuth
  reAuthenticate: disabled
  reAuthPeriod: 15                    <-- still 15
```

```
pcap -> /tmp/authm1304/T33374-S3.pcap (6 EAPOL frames)
     0.003 -> EAPOL-Start ... 1.023 <- EAP-Success id=2
RESULT T33374-S3-REMOVED-no-auth-reauthentication: 1/1 matched -- MATCH
```

**STEP 4 verdict: PASS.** **6 EAPOL frames in 76 seconds** -- identical to the STEP 0 control, in
a window that would have carried **five** re-authentications had the timer still been armed. The
line is gone from `show running-config` and `reAuthenticate` reads `disabled`. **The period on its
own does nothing; it is `auth reauthentication` that arms the timer.**

## Restore, and proof of it

```
configure terminal / interface port1.0.48 / no auth timeout reauth-period / end
```

`show running-config interface port1.0.48` is back to the four baseline lines exactly:

```
interface port1.0.48
 switchport
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 48
 dot1x port-control auto
 dot1x control-direction both
```

`show auth interface port1.0.48` is back to the group B baseline in every field:
`portStatus: Unauthorized`, **`reAuthenticate: disabled`**, **`reAuthPeriod: 3600`**,
quietPeriod 60, hostMode single-host, **CD adminControlledDirections: both**, dynamicVlanCreation
/ multiVlanSession / twoStepAuthentication / authMac / authWeb all disabled, supplicantMac none.

- **Nothing was written to startup-config.** No `write` was run; boot config is still
  `flash:/default.cfg`.
- **vlan 60, vlan 10, vlan 48 untouched.** No VLAN was added or removed.
- **Group A's rig left in place** for the rest of group B (that is the group contract).
- **`auth host-mode` was never touched in this case**, so the standing
  `control-direction`-rewrite finding could not apply here; `CD: both` was read back anyway and
  is correct.
- Nothing of ours left running on the box: every `eapol.py` run exited on its own
  (`--settle`-bounded) and each printed its RESULT line.

