(STANDING-ORDERS §8); it is well inside the noise group A saw in both directions on this unit.

One log line worth naming so nobody chases it: `IMISH[10482]: Command [end] failed` at 02:18:17
UTC. That is the known AW+ behaviour where `terminal`/`end` is exec-only and a queued send lands
in the wrong mode (memory `terminal-monitor-exec-only`); it came from a console tool's own
cleanup, not from a case step, and nothing depended on it.

## Not run, and why

- **Persistence across a reboot was NOT measured.** Proving it needs `write`, and **this group's
  restore contract is that `startup-config` stays `flash:/default.cfg` so that a reload is itself
  a complete restore** of group A's rig, which groups C and D inherit. Writing the rig to
  startup-config would have destroyed that property. The feature's configuration was proved to
  **appear in and disappear from `show running-config`**, which is the part that can be shown
  without compromising the bench. Recorded here so the gap is visible rather than implied.
- The `dot1x reauthentication` / `dot1x timeout re-authperiod` legacy spellings were not
  exercised; the dispatch named the `auth ...` forms and those are what TPS row 215 describes.

## VERDICT: PASS -- re-authentication occurs, on time, at the configured period, and stops when removed

`auth reauthentication` + `auth timeout reauth-period` work exactly as specified on
`sin_x96056-20261019-27`. Measured on the wire, never from `show`:
**OFF 6 frames / 1 authentication in 106 s; at 30 s, 26 frames and four re-authentications at
30.049, 30.044, 30.048, 30.049 s; at 60 s, 16 frames and intervals 60.070 and 60.068 s; at 15 s,
31 frames and six authentications at 15.03 s spacing** -- the count is a straight function of the
configured period. The authenticator **initiates** each cycle unsolicited, runs a **full** EAP
exchange with a **fresh challenge and new EAP ids** every time, and the **session never drops**
(port `Authorized` and supplicant `Authenticated` at four samples across the window). The DUT's
own RADIUS server counted **+6 Successes** for the six authentications seen on the wire, to the
unit. `no auth reauthentication` returns the port to **6 frames in 76 s with the period still
configured**, so the removal is real. Fully restored and verified field by field; health CLEAN
against the pre-existing dirty baseline.
